# .NET Architecture Standards

- Build and maintain this project as a C#/.NET codebase.
- Target .NET 10 and C# 14 for new code and updates unless explicitly instructed otherwise.
- Apply SOLID principles to keep responsibilities clear and dependencies well-structured.
- Follow DRY: extract reusable logic and avoid duplicated behavior across modules.
- Use dependency injection and interface-driven design at architectural boundaries.
- Keep classes and methods focused, cohesive, and small enough to be easy to reason about.
- Use current .NET and C# best practices, favoring framework-supported patterns over custom reinvention.
